<title>CANADA: Canada M1 money supply rises in May.</title>
<headline>Canada M1 money supply rises in May.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian M1 money supply rose by C$1.39 billion to C$71.01 billion in May from C$69.62 billion in April, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>					   May 97     Apr 97     May 96</p>
<p>M1					  71.01	69.62	61.02</p>
<p>M2					 391.85     391.14     391.67</p>
<p>M3					 509.56     505.39     485.14</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>   Chartered bank assets			 May	   Apr</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-14.59	-17.29</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     713.98	707.80</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    102.60	105.66</p>
<p>				    Wk to Jun 18  Chg on wk  Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  27.700  -0.055     +1.058</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     7.273  +2.604     +0.278</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	463.443  +2.250     -2.283</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 123.200  -1.200    -38.200</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  32.364  -0.049     -2.283</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745))</p>
</text>
